    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"img/header-image.png\" alt=\"dsh-webstack banner\" width=\"100%\" />\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <strong>Enterprise-Grade Web Search & Retrieval Plugin for DeepSeek Harness (<code>ctx.web</code>)</strong>\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://nodejs.org\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/node-%3E%3D22.18.0-blue.svg?style=flat-square\" alt=\"Node.js version\" /></a>\n  <a href=\"https://www.typescriptlang.org\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/typescript-5.7-blue.svg?style=flat-square\" alt=\"TypeScript\" /></a>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/QuantumKuba/dsh-webstack\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/cordis-ready-4A154B.svg?style=flat-square\" alt=\"Cordis Ready\" /></a>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/QuantumKuba/dsh-webstack\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/tests-35%20passing-success.svg?style=flat-square\" alt=\"Tests\" /></a>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/QuantumKuba/dsh-webstack\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/security-preflight%20SSRF%20hardened-brightgreen.svg?style=flat-square\" alt=\"Security\" /></a>\n  <a href=\"LICENSE\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-informational.svg?style=flat-square\" alt=\"License\" /></a>\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Overview",
      "text": "**`dsh-webstack`** is a high-performance web capability bundle for **DeepSeek Harness**, integrating **SearXNG** for metasearch discovery and **Scrapling** for multi-tier, anti-bot resilient content retrieval.\n\nEngineered specifically for local reasoning models (such as **Qwen 2.5/3.8 27B** and **DeepSeek R1/V3**) operating within bounded context windows (32k–90k tokens), `dsh-webstack` delivers web autonomy without tool bloat, context pollution, or security vulnerabilities."
    },
    {
      "section": "Overview",
      "text": "```\n                  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                  │                 DeepSeek Harness Agent                    │\n                  │             Local LLM (Qwen 3.8 27B / R1)                 │\n                  └─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "1. Zero Model-Facing Tool Bloat",
      "text": "The model interacts exclusively with the native DeepSeek Harness `web_search` and `web_fetch` schema. Advanced scraping parameters, stealth flags, and DNS checks remain entirely encapsulated inside the provider layer."
    },
    {
      "section": "2. Multi-Tier Retrieval Pipeline (`scrapling`)",
      "text": "Content fetching automatically scales across three performance tiers based on target complexity:"
    },
    {
      "section": "2. Multi-Tier Retrieval Pipeline (`scrapling`)",
      "text": "| Tier | Engine / Technology | Latency (Mean) | Primary Target |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| **Tier 1 (Default)** | `curl_cffi` (Chrome TLS fingerprint) | **531ms** | Documentation, GitHub, Wikipedia, blogs, REST endpoints |\n| **Tier 2 (Dynamic)** | Playwright Headless Chrome | **2,088ms** | Client-rendered JavaScript SPAs (React, Vue, Next.js) |\n| **Tier 3 (Stealth)** | `StealthyFetcher` Anti-Bot Engine | **1,669ms** | Cloudflare Turnstile, interstitials, anti-bot WAF challenges |"
    },
    {
      "section": "2. Multi-Tier Retrieval Pipeline (`scrapling`)",
      "text": "* **Turnstile Solver**: Automatic detection and click-coordinate humanization for interactive Cloudflare challenges.\n* **Fingerprint Camouflage**: Chromium canvas noise injection, WebRTC IP leakage suppression, genuine WebGL contexts, Google Search referer spoofing, and tracker blocking (~3,500 domains)."
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Kernel-Grade SSRF & Safe-URL Shield",
      "text": "All fetch requests undergo pre-flight DNS address validation prior to connection dispatch:\n* **Private Subnet Denial**: Immediately blocks loopback (`127.0.0.0/8`, `::1`), RFC 1918 subnets, link-local / cloud metadata endpoints (`169.254.169.254`), and carrier-grade NAT (`100.64.0.0/10`).\n* **Split-Horizon Protection**: Hostnames resolving to mixed public/private addresses are rejected immediately.\n* **Strict Same-Origin Redirects**: Redirects crossing origins or protocols are terminated with `WEB_REDIRECT_BLOCKED`.\n* **Zero-DNS Latency Penalty**: Security checks complete in **< 0.2ms** before any TCP handshake or sidecar dispatch."
    },
    {
      "section": "4. Context Optimization for Local LLMs",
      "text": "* **73.1% Token Reduction**: Raw HTML is converted to clean, semantic GitHub-Flavored Markdown via Harness's built-in Turndown pipeline.\n* **3.72x Effective Capacity**: Enables local 27B models to intake nearly 4x more documentation without exceeding context bounds or suffering attention dilution.\n* **Hard Output Bounds**: `fetchMaxOutputChars` capped at 50,000 characters to prevent context blowout."
    },
    {
      "section": "5. Zero-Leak Process Supervisor",
      "text": "* **Dynamic Loopback Binding**: The Python micro-sidecar binds to an OS-allocated ephemeral port (`127.0.0.1:0`) and handshakes readiness via JSON stdout (`{\"status\": \"ready\", \"port\": ..., \"pid\": ...}`).\n* **Fiber Teardown**: Hooks into Cordis lifecycle events to guarantee instantaneous termination (`1.5ms`) with zero orphan Python or Chromium processes.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Performance & Benchmark Highlights",
      "text": "Empirically validated on Apple Silicon (`Darwin arm64`) against local **SearXNG**, **Scrapling 0.4.7**, and **Qwen 3.8 27B** via oMLX:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Performance & Benchmark Highlights",
      "text": "| Dimension | Measured Metric | Target & Significance |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| **SearXNG Search Latency** | **1,148ms** mean / **1,736ms** P95 | **100% success rate** across technical API, debugging, and general queries |\n| **Fast HTTP Fetch (Tier 1)** | **531ms** mean / **687ms** P95 | High-throughput documentation retrieval with browser TLS impersonation |\n| **Stealth Anti-Bot Fetch (Tier 3)** | **1,669ms** mean | Solves Cloudflare Turnstile & interstitial challenges autonomously |\n| **Context Token Savings** | **73.1% reduction** (3.72x multiplier) | Compresses ~32.6k raw HTML tokens down to ~8.8k semantic GFM tokens |\n| **SSRF Threat Prevention** | **100% intercepted** (8/8 attack vectors) | < 0.2ms abort decision; zero network requests dispatched to private nets |\n| **Bridge Startup / Teardown** | **114.7ms** boot / **1.5ms** exit | Dynamic ephemeral port assignment; **0 orphan/zombie processes** |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Performance & Benchmark Highlights",
      "text": "> 📊 *For complete per-query distributions, latency variance, and test setups, refer to the [Benchmark Report](benchmark/BENCHMARK_REPORT.md).*\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "1. Install Plugin",
      "text": "```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "In your DeepSeek Harness workspace:",
      "text": "pnpm add dsh-webstack"
    },
    {
      "section": "or via npm",
      "text": "npm install dsh-webstack\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "2. Configure SearXNG & Scrapling",
      "text": "* **SearXNG**: Deploy via Docker Compose with JSON enabled on `http://127.0.0.1:8080` (see [SearXNG Setup Guide](docs/searxng-setup.md)).\n* **Scrapling**: Install into a virtual environment with stealth extras (see [Scrapling Setup Guide](docs/scrapling-setup.md)):\n  ```bash\n  pip install \"scrapling[stealth]\" && playwright install chromium\n  ```"
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Mount Cordis Patch Layer",
      "text": "Apply `cordis.patch.yml` to your DeepSeek Harness profile to connect `ctx.web`:\n```yaml\n- id: web\n  config:\n    searchProvider: searxng\n    fetchProvider: scrapling\n\n---"
    },
    {
